## Pros and Cons — Marquise Moissanite Ring

**Pros:**
- **75–92% savings vs natural diamond** at every carat weight. A 2ct complete ring at ~$3,299 vs ~$17,350 for a natural 2ct equivalent.
- **50–62% savings vs lab diamond** at 1–3ct. Moissanite stone prices plateau — no 2ct or 3ct price cliff the way lab diamonds have.
- **Maximum face-up per dollar.** A 2ct marquise moissanite at ~$11.5x5.8mm face-up costs ~$949. A 2ct lab diamond at the same dimensions costs $2,212. Same visual size, 57% less.
- **9.25 Mohs hardness.** Hard enough for daily wear without special maintenance. Second hardest engagement ring material.
- **High fire and brilliance.** If you love rainbow fire, moissanite is the maximum-fire choice at any price. Nothing in the engagement ring market produces more colored fire per carat.
- **No resale anxiety.** Moissanite and lab diamonds both depreciate significantly. Neither is bought for resale. The pressure to "invest" in the stone does not apply.

**Cons:**
- **Visible rainbow fire — not for everyone.** The 2.4x Fire Gap is a feature for some buyers and a dealbreaker for others. Setting choice moderates it. Nothing eliminates it.
- **Reads as moissanite to observers who know jewelry.** Any gemologist or experienced jeweler identifies moissanite instantly. If passing as diamond matters, choose lab diamond.
- **Camera amplification is not removable.** Your ring will always photograph more rainbow than it looks in person. This surprises buyers who expected it to look "normal" in photos.
- **No resale market.** Moissanite has essentially no secondary market value. Buy it to wear it.
- **Bow-tie risk still applies.** Marquise cut moissanite carries the same bow-tie shadow risk as a marquise diamond. Always watch the 360° video of the specific stone. See our [marquise diamond bow-tie guide](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie).
- **Tip protection is critical.** The pointed marquise tips chip the same way on moissanite as on diamond. Use a six-prong or bezel setting. See our [marquise bezel engagement ring guide](/marquise-bezel-engagement-ring).

> **"For clients on a real budget who want a 2ct marquise ring, I always lay out the moissanite path. The math is hard to argue with. A $3,299 total ring vs $4,562 for the lab diamond equivalent — same shape, same setting, same face-up size. The difference is the fire character and $1,263. I've never had a client regret the moissanite choice when they understood the fire going in. The ones who feel surprised are the ones nobody told about the Fire Gap beforehand."** — Farzana Hasan, Diamond Expert

