## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is a marquise moissanite ring?

**A marquise moissanite ring uses a moissanite centre stone cut in the marquise (boat/eye) shape.** It delivers the same elongated, finger-slimming silhouette as a marquise diamond at 75–92% less cost. A 1ct marquise moissanite ring starts at ~$2,069 complete. A 1ct natural diamond equivalent starts at $6,620+.

### How much does a marquise moissanite ring cost?

**$2,069–$3,799 for a complete ring at 1–3ct.** Stone prices: ~$449 (1ct), ~$949 (2ct), ~$1,449 (3ct) for Forever One DEF from Charles & Colvard. Ring settings from certified market inventory run $1,620–$2,550. Add stone + setting for total ring cost. A natural diamond equivalent ring runs $6,620–$27,350+.

### Does marquise moissanite look fake?

**It does not look fake — it looks like moissanite.** An observer who knows diamonds will recognize the rainbow fire pattern immediately. An observer who does not know diamonds sees a brilliant, colorful stone. Moissanite does not look like cubic zirconia. It fires more intensely than diamond, not less. Whether the fire reads as "better than diamond" or "obviously not diamond" varies by observer.

### What are the 3 fire differences between moissanite and lab diamond?

**1. Indoors** — moissanite fires rainbow on every movement; lab diamond fires mostly white. **2. Outdoors in sunlight** — moissanite shows full-spectrum "disco ball" effect; lab diamond fires intense white with occasional color. **3. In photos** — smartphones amplify moissanite fire 2–3x vs naked eye; lab diamond photos amplify less. The Fire Gap (0.104 vs 0.044 dispersion) is the source of all three differences.

### Is marquise moissanite harder than a diamond?

**No — diamond (10 Mohs) is harder than moissanite (9.25 Mohs).** For daily engagement ring wear, both are effectively scratch-proof. No gemstone except diamond will scratch moissanite at 9.25 Mohs. The 0.75 Mohs gap matters in extreme abrasion conditions, not in normal wear.

### What color grade should I pick for marquise moissanite?

**Forever One DEF.** The marquise's long face-up surface amplifies color at the pointed ends. G-H range moissanite shows yellow-green tint in white gold or platinum at 2ct+. DEF range (~$449 at 1ct) looks clean in any metal. The $50–$100 premium per carat is worth it. See our [marquise diamond color guide](/marquise-diamond-color-guide) for the same principle on diamonds.

### What setting is best for a marquise moissanite ring?

**Three stone with diamond flankers in rose or yellow gold.** Diamond flankers split fire attention between the moissanite centre and the flanker sparkle. Warm metal tones the fire toward amber-warm rather than electric-rainbow. Entry pick: [Three Stone in 14k Rose Gold at $1,620](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315101?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (133 reviews).

### Is marquise moissanite good for daily wear?

**Yes, with the right setting.** At 9.25 Mohs, moissanite resists scratching for daily wear. The main consideration is tip protection — marquise points are the same chip risk as a diamond marquise. Use a six-prong or bezel setting for daily wear. See our [marquise bezel engagement ring guide](/marquise-bezel-engagement-ring) for full protection options.

### How does marquise moissanite compare to oval moissanite?

**Marquise delivers more face-up area per carat and a stronger finger-slimming effect.** At 2ct, a marquise measures ~11.5x5.8mm vs an oval at ~10.5x7mm. The marquise is longer and narrower — more dramatic on the finger. The fire difference applies equally to both shapes. See our [oval vs marquise diamond](/oval-vs-marquise-diamond) comparison for shape analysis.

### Do I need a certificate for a marquise moissanite ring?

**No — moissanite does not use GIA or IGI certification.** [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/) grades diamonds, not moissanite. Charles & Colvard's Forever One grade is manufacturer-certified. You receive a C&C certificate confirming the stone grade. If you pair a lab diamond centre stone, verify the IGI certificate at [igi.org](https://www.igi.org/) before purchase.

### Can a marquise moissanite ring pass as a diamond?

**To most people, yes. To a jeweler, no.** A diamond tester distinguishes moissanite from diamond. A jeweler examining the fire pattern will recognize moissanite at once. Most daily social observers will not have a tester and will not know the difference. If the goal is to pass a professional's examination, lab diamond is the correct choice.

### What carat size is best for a marquise moissanite ring?

**1.5–2ct for most finger sizes.** At 1ct, the marquise face-up is ~8.5x4.3mm — noticeable but not dominant. At 2ct (~11.5x5.8mm), it fills the finger and maximizes the elongating effect without looking oversized on a normal hand. At 3ct (~13x6.5mm), it becomes a bold statement piece. See our [marquise diamond size chart](/marquise-cut-diamond-size-chart) for the full size stack.

### Where does moissanite rainbow fire come from?

**From its dispersion coefficient — 0.104 for moissanite vs 0.044 for diamond.** Dispersion measures how much the stone bends different light wavelengths at different angles, separating white light into its component colors. Moissanite's 0.104 is 2.4x diamond's 0.044. The marquise's long flat table amplifies this effect across a larger surface than shorter shapes.

### Should I choose moissanite or lab diamond for a marquise ring?

**Moissanite if fire character is acceptable and savings matter. Lab diamond if diamond fire character is the priority.** The price gap at 1ct is $350–$750 for the complete ring. At 2ct, it is $1,263. At 3ct, it is $2,370. If the Fire Gap is not a dealbreaker, moissanite gives you more stone for less at every carat weight. See our [lab grown marquise diamond guide](/lab-grown-marquise-diamond) for lab diamond pricing as the comparison baseline.

